{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Page
  Phase 10. The template every /pages/<handle> URL resolves to.

  Sources of truth:
  - PHASE-1-WEBSITE-AUDIT.md SHOP-09, which sections/main-cart.liquid records as
    the finding that Shopify serves an error page for any storefront route whose
    template is missing, and which lists "page" among the templates still
    missing after Phase 8. This file removes it from that list.
  - PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §26.2 (measure) and §14.4 (the 60-75 character
    reading target), as assets/section-our-story.css records them.

  IT IS THE DESTINATION THE THEME ALREADY POINTS AT.
  sections/our-story.liquid tells the merchant, in the button_url info string,
  to "Create the page in Shopify admin first, then select it here." Until this
  file existed that instruction led to an error page, and so did every link to a
  size guide, a shipping page, a returns page or an About page.

  SHOPIFY IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH, AND HERE IT IS THE MERCHANT'S PROSE.
  There is no copy in this file. The title is page.title and the body is
  page.content — merchant HTML from the Shopify rich-text editor, rendered
  as it stands. The theme styles those elements; it never writes, edits,
  truncates or reorders a word of them. No About text, no policy, no shipping
  claim and no scripture is invented here.

  THE TITLE IS HIDDEN, NEVER REMOVED.
  "Show the page title" is a visibility setting, not a rendering one. A merchant
  whose rich text already opens with its own title wants one heading on the
  screen, not none in the document: dropping the h1 would leave the page with no
  level-1 heading at all, which is the outline defect Phase 1 HTML-03 records,
  and their own first heading would be left hanging at whatever level they chose
  with nothing above it. So the h1 always renders and the setting adds the
  visually-hidden utility to it, which keeps it in the accessibility tree and
  out of the picture.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE.
  No breadcrumb — a page has no parent in this theme's navigation and inventing
  a trail would mean inventing a hierarchy. No share row, no author, no date, no
  "last updated", no table of contents, no related pages, no page image banner.
  Each is either a business fact nobody has supplied or a composition that would
  have to be undone by whichever phase owns it; this surface's job is to present
  merchant prose, not to add a second voice above it.

  THIS main-* SECTION DOES CARRY SPACING SETTINGS, WHICH main-cart AND
  main-product DO NOT.
  On those two the page rhythm is fixed because the page is one composition that
  Shopify's own templates never extend. templates/page.json is different: a
  merchant can and will add sections beneath this one — a collection row under a
  size guide, an Our Story band under an About page — so where the prose band
  stops is a composition decision that belongs to them. The surface select is
  exposed for the same reason main-product exposes one: both cream and ink carry
  body copy at 17.04:1 in design-tokens.css §2, so neither is disqualified.

  ZERO JavaScript.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign show_heading = section.settings.show_heading

  assign surface_class = 'surface-light'
  if section.settings.surface == 'dark'
    assign surface_class = 'surface-dark'
  endif

  comment
    The title's class string is built here so the markup stays a straight render
    with no control flow in it. visually-hidden is the utility defined once in
    assets/header.css, which layout/theme.liquid loads on every page; this
    composes it rather than shipping a second copy of the clip recipe.
  endcomment
  assign title_classes = 'main-page__title'
  if show_heading == false
    assign title_classes = title_classes | append: ' visually-hidden'
  endif

  assign classes = 'main-page '
  assign classes = classes | append: surface_class
  assign classes = classes | append: ' main-page--pt-' | append: section.settings.spacing_top
  assign classes = classes | append: ' main-page--pb-' | append: section.settings.spacing_bottom
  comment
    A derived-state modifier. The gap between the title and the prose cannot be
    set on the title: visually-hidden takes the h1 out of flow, where a margin
    does nothing. It sits on the prose instead — which means it outlives the
    hidden title, and this modifier is what takes it away, so the band does not
    open with 40px of nothing.
  endcomment
  if show_heading == false
    assign classes = classes | append: ' main-page--no-heading'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  No render guard, and the stylesheet link is therefore unwrapped at the top of
  the file. A template-bound section always renders: there is no unconfigured
  state to cost a request, because the page exists or the route does not.

  No header-clearance rule either, here or in the stylesheet. The Phase 4
  header only overlays its first section when template.name == 'index'
  (sections/header.liquid), so on a page template it is in normal flow and
  --header-overlay-offset is never published.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'section-main-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="{{ classes }}" {{ section.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="main-page__inner container">
    <div class="main-page__column">
      <h1 class="{{ title_classes }}">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>

      {%- if page.content != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Merchant HTML, output as it stands. It is not passed through strip_html
          — the formatting is the point — and it is not escaped, because Shopify
          sanitises rich-text content on save and escaping it here would render
          the merchant's own tags as visible text.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="main-page__content">{{ page.content }}</div>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Theme Editor only. A titled page with no body is a state a merchant
          reaches by creating the page and not yet writing it, and on the live
          storefront it is simply a short page rather than an error — so the
          note is never shown to a customer.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="main-page__notice">{{ 'sections.main_page.no_content' | t }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Page",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "main-page-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The title and the text come from the page itself, in Shopify admin under Online Store > Pages. Nothing on this page is written in the theme."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_heading",
      "label": "Show the page title",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Turn this off only when your page text already opens with its own title. The title is still read out by screen readers and still counts as the page's first-level heading — it is hidden from view, not removed. Inside the page text, start at Heading 2: Heading 1 belongs to the title, and the theme cannot change the level of text you have already written."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "surface",
      "label": "Colour scheme",
      "info": "Cream is the default, as it is on the product page. Long text is legible on both; the theme switches text, border, accent and focus colours to suit whichever you choose.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Cream" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Ink" }
      ],
      "default": "light"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The text sits in a single reading column and stays there on the widest screen, inside the 60 to 75 characters a line the design system targets. Line length is what makes long text readable, so it is not a setting."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_top",
      "label": "Space above",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "spacing_bottom",
      "label": "Space below",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "tight", "label": "Tight" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "Standard" }
      ],
      "default": "standard",
      "info": "Set this to None when you add another section directly beneath this one and want the two to meet."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["page"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
